### Click ▶ next to a request to run it. Requests are separated by ###.
### Run them from top to bottom: the POST saves the new id in {{elevId}}.
### Kafka (elev-infra) and elev-service must be running.

### 1. Create a student -> 202 Accepted
POST http://localhost:8080/elever
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "navn": "Ola Nordmann",
  "klasse": "10A"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("elevId", response.body.id);
    client.test("Status is 202", () => client.assert(response.status === 202));
%}

### 2. Get all students -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/elever

### 3. Get the student created in request 1 -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/elever/{{elevId}}

### 4. Unknown id -> 404
GET http://localhost:8080/elever/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 5. Blank name -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/elever
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "navn": "",
  "klasse": "10A"
}

### 6. Stop elev-service and run this -> 503
GET http://localhost:8080/elever

### 7. Health
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health
